    "payload": {
      "content": "When reviewing papers that do not introduce new algorithms (ORIG-MTH weakness), assess originality primarily through novel problem formulations (ORIG-PROB) and empirical insights (ORIG-ANL). A key strength is identifying previously unaddressed trade-offs or limitations in existing architectures (ORIG-NEG). However, originality is weakened if experimental setups are limited to simple benchmarks (e.g., MNIST) without validation on complex datasets (ORIG-EXP weakness). Ensure that the combination of existing techniques (ORIG-COM) is well-motivated by the intersection of distinct research lines. For empirical-only papers, the value lies in the depth of the insight provided about known methods rather than the novelty of the method itself.",
